    note: "Drive day from the Camargue to the Languedoc coast at Marseillan-Plage. Morning in the Camargue (flamingos at Pont-de-Gau before you leave), then a coastal drive to Sete for Halles de Sete market (fresh fish for camp cooking) and Chez Alphonse ice cream. Arrive at Camping Beauregard Plage, direct beach access for the afternoon."
  - day_id: "day_2026-06-09"
    day_number: 6
    date: "2026-06-09"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJEcO6yQphthIRA39hbmBWb4U"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJEcO6yQphthIRA39hbmBWb4U"
    locked: false
    note: "Base day on the Languedoc coast. Morning brunch at La Fabrique a gout-the in Marseillan village, then Noilly Prat cellar tour (for adults while kids snack). Afternoon on the beach at Marseillan-Plage or a quick run to Sete for Halles de Sete and the Mont Saint-Clair viewpoint. Evening oysters on the Marseillan quay (Bassin de Thau is France's biggest oyster basin)."
  - day_id: "day_2026-06-10"
