    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJP2GhiMdSBQ0R0rI-WJg3XWQ"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJRSbc_S3lGQ0RXmF7SjJgumI"
    locked: false
    note: "Base day with the vehicle parked and nearby activity, food, and provisioning options."
  - day_id: "day_2026-06-29"
    day_number: 26
    date: "2026-06-29"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJRSbc_S3lGQ0RXmF7SjJgumI"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJRSbc_S3lGQ0RXmF7SjJgumI"
    locked: false
    note: "Direct inland route from Monte Gordo to Evora (skipping the SW Portugal coast we know well already). Short drive through Alentejo cork-oak country. Afternoon arrival leaves time to walk Evora's Roman temple and have dinner in the old town."
  - day_id: "day_2026-06-30"
    day_number: 27
    date: "2026-06-30"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJRSbc_S3lGQ0RXmF7SjJgumI"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJc0-KcqYKFg0R-Si5hXbKf2k"
    locked: false
    note: "Base day at Orbitur Evora. Morning in Evora (Roman temple, cathedral, Chapel of Bones, Mercado Municipal for provisions). Afternoon day trip to Monsaraz hilltop village and Esporao wine estate (kids-friendly terrace, olive oil and wine tasting for adults)."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-01"
    day_number: 28
    date: "2026-07-01"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJc0-KcqYKFg0R-Si5hXbKf2k"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJc0-KcqYKFg0R-Si5hXbKf2k"
    locked: false
    note: "Drive day to Extremadura. Cross into Spain via Elvas or Badajoz, continue to Caceres - one of the most complete medieval walled cities in Europe. Check in at Camping Caceres (private sanitary block per pitch is a rarity worth noting), then bus into the UNESCO old town for evening walk. Dinner at Borona Bistro if you reserve ahead."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-02"
    day_number: 29
    date: "2026-07-02"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJc0-KcqYKFg0R-Si5hXbKf2k"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJq268IYUlPw0Rplmt6tTIHGs"
    locked: false
    note: "Base day in Caceres. Two strong options: (1) morning at Monfrague National Park - eye-level vulture colonies at Salto del Gitano, kids love this - then Trujillo lunch at Dos Orillas (hidden courtyard restaurant); or (2) full day in Caceres old town exploring the stork-topped towers and stone lanes."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-03"
    day_number: 30
    date: "2026-07-03"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJq268IYUlPw0Rplmt6tTIHGs"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJ61Rfqm_QUQ0R8Syz4JbxGRo"
    locked: false
    note: "Shorter drive than before (220km vs original 390km from Evora). Option to detour via Monfrague if you didn't do it on the base day, or stop in Plasencia for lunch. Afternoon arrival in Salamanca with time for a proper Plaza Mayor evening."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-04"
    day_number: 31
    date: "2026-07-04"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJ61Rfqm_QUQ0R8Syz4JbxGRo"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJ61Rfqm_QUQ0R8Syz4JbxGRo"
    locked: false
    note: "Base day with the vehicle parked and nearby activity, food, and provisioning options."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-05"
    day_number: 32
    date: "2026-07-05"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJ61Rfqm_QUQ0R8Syz4JbxGRo"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
    locked: true
    note: "Drive day from Salamanca to the French Basque Country. The sleep location is Camping Bachoc a la Ferme (4.8 rating, farm setting) - a stronger match for the trip's aesthetic than wecamp San Sebastian. The scenic route takes you via Guernica (Gernika-Lumo) - the Basque parliament town, the oak tree, the historical weight of the place - and Getaria for txakoli and grilled fish at the harbour."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-06"
    day_number: 33
    date: "2026-07-06"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
    locked: true
    note: "Base day at Camping Bachoc a la Ferme. The French Basque coast is right there: Guethary for the small-scale, stylish surf-village feel; Saint-Jean-de-Luz for the sheltered family beach and harbour-town pastry; Espelette inland for the piment cooperative - a tin is one of the most useful camp buys of the trip."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-07"
    day_number: 34
    date: "2026-07-07"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
    sleep_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
    locked: true
    note: "Short drive day from the French Basque Country into the Landes. Already on the French side so the border crossing is behind you. Stop at Espelette for the piment cooperative before continuing, Capbreton for fresh fish at the harbour quay, then settle into Huttopia Landes Sud's pine forest setting."
  - day_id: "day_2026-07-08"
    day_number: 35
    date: "2026-07-08"
    wake_location_id: "location_ChIJ37rm3HJZUQ0R7PgZ5is0a24"
