    {
      "id": "location_ChIJ_4_BVJpPTg0RgJCoY5zXEDE",
      "name": "Guernica (Gernika-Lumo)",
      "description": "The most historically resonant town on the route. Market town in Biscay, seat of the Basque Parliament, home of the Gernikako Arbola (the ancient oak tree symbolising Basque freedoms), and the town bombed on 26 April 1937 that became the subject of Picasso's painting. A genuine half-day stop - not a drive-by.",
