    {
      "id": "location_ChIJD6krJVJ3UA0RjZvYiSj3CwE",
      "name": "Espelette",
      "description": "French Basque village famous for the AOP piment d'Espelette. A short detour off the D918 between San Sebastian and Biarritz. The Espelette pepper cooperative sells directly - a tin is one of the most useful camp-cooking buys on the whole trip. The village turns red in late summer when peppers hang to dry from every facade. Worth 45 minutes.",
